when was the movie to kill a mocking bird made,"['http://www.freegreatmovies.com/Free-Movie/To-Kill-a-Mockingbird/2833', 'https://www.historyandheadlines.com/december-25-1962-kill-mockingbird/', 'http://www.theheliosgallery.com/products-page-2-2/featured/mary-badham-and-gregory-peck-reading-script-set-portrait/', 'http://little-merlins-frangula.tk/to-kill-a-mockingbird-sheet-music.html', 'https://www.allaboutmovies.com.au/index.php/poster-formats/one-sheet-posters/item/109785-to-kill-a-mockingbird-poster-original-one-sheet-1962-gregory-peck-robert-mulligan', 'https://worldhistoryproject.org/2003/6/12/gregory-peck-dies', 'https://blog.enotes.com/2010/12/28/worst-and-best-books-to-film/']",To Kill a Mockingbird is a 1962 American drama film directed by Robert Mulligan. The screenplay by Horton Foote is based on Harper Lee's 1960 Pulitzer Prize-winning novel of the same name. It stars Gregory Peck as Atticus Finch and Mary Badham as Scout.,"Movie Description
To Kill a Mockingbird is a classic 1962 drama film directed by Robert Mulligan, based on Harper Lee's 1960 novel. Set in the 1930s Deep South, the story follows young Scout Finch and her brother Jem as they navigate the complexities of race, class, and morality in their small town. Their father, Atticus Finch, played by Gregory Peck, is a principled lawyer who defends a black man wrongfully accused of raping a white woman, facing racial prejudices and societal injustices head-on. Gregory Peck won an Oscar for Best Actor for his performance. It is considered one of the greatest American films of all time.
