what was the name of thierry’s original documentary,"['https://movieposters.wonderhowto.com/news/exit-through-gift-shop-2010-0122966/', 'http://www.documentarytube.com/videos/exit-through-the-gift-shop', 'https://nouw.com/dakotaleest/what-is-art-34435132', 'http://itspeakstudio.com/music-audio/exit-through-the-gift-shop-soundtrack.php', 'https://artcentermorrobay.org/', 'http://gluedtomatoes.com/exit-through-the-gift-shop-free.html', 'http://artlog.art50.net/art-movies/documentary-films/']","Exit Through the Gift Shop: A Banksy Film is a 2010 British documentary film, directed by street artist Banksy. It tells the story of Thierry Guetta, a French immigrant in Los Angeles, and his obsession with street art. The film charts Guetta's constant documenting of his every waking moment on film, from a chance encounter with his cousin, the artist Invader, to his introduction to a host of street artists with a focus on Shepard Fairey and Banksy, whose anonymity is preserved by obscuring his face and altering his voice, to Guetta's eventual fame as a street artist himself. It is narrated by Rhys Ifans. The music is by Geoff Barrow. It includes Richard Hawley's ""Tonight The Streets Are Ours"".","Here is the movie trailer for the Bansky film ""EXIT THROUGH THE GIFT SHOP""
