what does tight end position in football do,"['https://wikivisually.com/wiki/Ken_MacAfee', 'http://insidethepylon.com/nfl/teams-nfl/afc-east/new-england-patriots/2015/10/02/the-new-england-patriots-wham-schemes/', 'https://overthecap.com/projecting-the-rookie-escalators-and-top-performance-based-play-earners/']","Because of the hybrid nature of the position, the tight end's role in any given offense depends on the tactical preferences and philosophy of the head coach. In some systems, the tight end will merely act as a sixth offensive lineman, rarely going out for passes. Other systems use the tight end primarily as a receiver, frequently taking advantage of the tight end's size to create mismatches in the defensive secondary. Many coaches will often have one tight end who specializes in blocking in running situations while using a tight end with better pass-catching skills in obvious passing situations.","WikiVisually
