who is and what is the role of the lord mayor of the city of london,"['https://wikivisually.com/wiki/Aldersgate', 'https://www.passport-collector.com/the-passport-of-captain-francis-garratt/', 'https://questionsandancestors.blogspot.com/2014/06/', 'https://www.wanderlex.com/bank-oxford-circus/', 'https://www.answers.com/Q/FAQ/4906', 'https://www.addictionhelper.com/treatment/london/city-of-london/', 'http://markmueller.info/search?q=The%20secret%20city%20film']","The Lord Mayor of London is the City of London's mayor and leader of the City of London Corporation. Within the City, the Lord Mayor is accorded precedence over all individuals except the sovereign and retains various traditional powers, rights and privileges, including the title and style The Right Honourable the Lord Mayor of London.","Aldersgate is a Ward of the City of London, England, named after one of the northern gates in the London Wall which once enclosed the City.
