what is a duty placed on goods that are imported or exported,"['https://wikivisually.com/wiki/Foreign_direct_investment', 'https://www.mahanyertl.com/customs-duties-tariffs/', 'https://www.palkhi.com/faq/?setCurrencyId=3', 'https://www.nallucollection.com/faq/', 'https://cargofromchina.com/landed-cost/', 'https://www.paltrade.org/en_US/page/customs-valuation-and-classification', 'http://up-us.info/2018/09']","A customs duty or due is the indirect tax levied on the import or export of goods in international trade. In economic sense, a duty is also a kind of consumption tax. A duty levied on goods being imported is referred to as an import duty. Similarly, a duty levied on exports is called an export duty. A tariff, which is actually a list of commodities along with the leviable rate (amount) of customs duty, is popularly referred to as a customs duty.","WikiVisually
