another name for a central processing unit is a,"['https://www.qyresearch.com/expert/xdetail/636/global-processor-market', 'http://www.mentorforbankexams.com/2017/10/central-processing-unit-parts-definition-function.html', 'https://wikivisually.com/wiki/Central_processing_unit', 'http://www.banktheories.com/2017/02/computing-in-banking.html', 'http://dcjtech.info/topic/over-five-types-of-computers-explained-and-compared/', 'https://www.workingdreamers.com/idea/eb77686dc063252706ba9d4c8b65dadfece9ab84', 'https://eng.kakprosto.ru/how-901137-multi-core-processors-principles-of-operation-']","Most modern CPUs are microprocessors, meaning they are contained on a single integrated circuit (IC) chip. An IC that contains a CPU may also contain memory, peripheral interfaces, and other components of a computer; such integrated devices are variously called microcontrollers or systems on a chip (SoC). Some computers employ a multi-core processor, which is a single chip containing two or more CPUs called ""cores""; in that context, one can speak of such single chips as ""sockets"".","Market Research Reports & Industry Insights | 2007-Present - QY Research-QYResearch Sorry,Page Not FoundYou can try to search for product words or fill in the following information to leave a message, we will contact you as soon as possible by *Required lnformation WORLD WIDE OFFICE [SEP_DOC] A central processing unit (CPU), also called a central processor, main processor, or just processor, is the most important processor in a given computer. Its electronic circuitry executes instructions of a computer program, such as arithmetic, logic, controlling, and input/output (I/O) operations. This role contrasts with that of external components, such as main memory and I/O circuitry, and specialized coprocessors such as graphics processing units (GPUs).
Inside a central processing unit: The integrated circuit of Intel's Xeon 3060, first manufactured in 2006
