Nunez Genealogy & History
Nunez is a surname of Hispanic origins. It is a patronymic (derived from the father's given name) from ""Nu?o"" and the suffix ""ez"". Nunez genealogy shows that this surname first appeared in Castile, Spain, which was a powerful Christian kingdom in medieval Spain. A famous person in Nunez family history was Vasco Nunez de Balboa, the first European to see the Pacific Ocean. Other prominent people with this last name include Eduardo Nunez, who plays first base for the New York Yankees; and Fabian Nunez, who is the former speaker of the California assembly and still prominent in state politics.
