Quick Information
Aimee Mann is one of the popular American rock singer, guitarist, bassist and singer-songwriter born on September 8, 1960. Mann has performed as a solo musician since the band 'Til Tuesday broke up where she was the bassist and a vocalist. Till the day, Mann has released many of her songs and albums, which are, continue hits. She is believed to earn a net worth of $ 4 million. Mann has number of fans and followers following her through different social net working sites. She is able to make her place n the world of entertainment with the hard work, dedication and commitment.
Moving on to her early life, she was born in Bon Air, Virginia. Mann was talented since her childhood days. She was very good in her studies and equally showed her interest in music. Mann graduated from Open High School situated in Richmond, Virginia. In order to pursue her career in music, she joined Berklee College of Music in Boston, Massachusetts. In the mean while, Mann joined the Boston punk band The Young Snakes. Mann with the band released the EP Bark Along with The Young Snakes in the year 1983, which was the opening of her career.
With the boyfriend Michael Hausman, Mann co-founded the new wave band 'Til Tuesday in the year 1983. The band released Voices Carry in the year 1985 which won the MTV Video Music Award for Best New Artist. The band released their second album Welcome Home in 1986. She sang vocals with Geddy Lee on ""Time Stand Still"" and also appeared in the video in the year 1987. The band released their third and final album Everything's Different Now in 1988. When Mann left to start her solo career, the band broke up in the year 1990. Then after, Aimee Mann released her album, whatever in the year 1993. She released her second album I'm with Stupid in 1995.
In this way Mann began her solo career. Slowly and gradually, she sang many songs and released many albums. She has also been nominated for many awards like Grammy Award and academy award. Magnolia, Bachelor no 2, Live at St. Ann's Warehouse, The Forgotten Arm, One More Drifter in the Snow, @#%&*! Smilers etc are some of her albums, which helped her to establish as a rock singer in the music industry.
Throughout her career, she not only has sung many songs and had a tour for her concerts but also has appeared in television and films. She also has appeared in Independent Music Awards as a judging panel. In the year 1997, Mann married songwriter Michael Penn after dating him for a long time. Her husband supported her a lot in her journey towards success. As he has been a loving husband and a caring father to her children, she says her to be blessed to have him in her life. She has never imagined about having a divorce with him.
