Kalamata Street Art festival has been my first volunteer and it was unforgettable. I went with quite high expectations and it has exceeded them. This experience has allowed me to meet and live with people from different countries and therefore, different custom, cultures, personalities… Which makes you develop the most empathic/understandable, social, etc. part of you. The organization of the festival joined us and we created a great team. Unfortunately, after hard work, we could celebrate only one day of the festival. However, it was awesome because we could see the result of what we have been working on and it was the moment to enjoy it. You have to be prepared to expect the unexpected and know how to adapt and
solve problems. The word that sums up for me this little adventure is ROLLER-COASTER (It means that you have good moments and others not so much, even so, one always repeat).
