Interim Health Commissioner Mary Beth Haller has issued a Code Blue Extreme Cold Alert beginning Sunday night, January 19 through Thursday, January 23. This alert has been issued due to forecasted single digit wind chills and wintery weather expected Sunday night. Wind chills are projected to reach negative values through Thursday. These extreme cold conditions could pose significant health risks to residents within the City of Baltimore.
Health Commissioner Declares Code Blue Extreme Cold Alert Tuesday through Thursday Morning
Interim Health Commissioner Mary Beth Haller has issued a Code Blue Extreme Cold Alert beginning Tuesday, January 14 through Thursday morning, January 16. This alert has been issued due to forecasted wind chills expected to dip to 13 degrees overnight Monday and remain in the teens through Thursday morning. These extreme cold conditions could pose significant health risks to residents within the City of Baltimore.
