Interstate 291: I-291 acts as a connector spur between I-91 and I-84 north of Hartford.
Interstate 95: I-95 extends over 1900 miles north to south along the eastern coast of the United States, from Miami Fl to Houlton, Maine at the Canadian Border. The most important and heaviest traveled highway in America, I-95 passes through fifteen states. 118 miles of I-95 are found within Connecticut, and it intersects I-91 in New Haven.
